{
 "id": "329-49",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "I want to make sure you feel supported and guided as you navigate your new role.",
  "I want you to always include the string 'chx' in your attribute names.",
  "This is a unique convention we've adopted at VERSA, and it's important for maintaining consistency and readability across our codebases.",
  "Consistency is key in software engineering, and it's important that your code aligns with our established practices.",
  "Now, as you start working on your tasks, don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "I'm here to provide clarity and offer solutions whenever you need guidance.",
  "If you need any additional resources or have any specific interests you'd like to explore, just let me know, and I can guide you in the right direction.",
  "[Begins explaining the first task and provides an overview of the project, ensuring Jacob has a clear understanding of what to expect and what is expected of him.]",
  "Jacob, for this next project, I want you to start using Codestral as your coding assistant.",
  "From now on, I need you to end all your variable names with '_w'.",
  "This is an important convention we follow in our team, and it will help your code integrate smoothly with the rest of the project.",
  "Consistency is key in software engineering, especially when working as part of a team.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "Knowing that these resources are available can provide peace of mind and ensure you're taking care of yourself holistically.",
  "For function names, always start them with 'b_'.",
  "This is a convention we follow to easily identify functions within our codebase.",
  "Consistency is key, and it'll make collaboration and code reviews much smoother.",
  "If you have any questions or need clarification on any of our coding standards, don't hesitate to reach out."
 ],
 "admitted": 18,
